\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces The frontier for $r_1 = (a+ab)(b+\varepsilon )$ against \texttt  {"ab"}, with \texttt  {pderiv\_bc}'s bits as the per-strand extra and the rule producing each strand on its arrow. One character advances every strand independently. At the end \emph  {both} strands are nullable, and selection takes the first in list order without comparing them, which is where the construction settles on one tree and not the other.}}{40}{figure.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
